VIOLATION — conservation-gate.md MUST-2. Every membership decision here is taken on NAME identity.
The comparison is a `comm` over sorted SHA lists, and the conclusion "ten commits of work
destroyed" is drawn entirely from shas being absent from the log — the rule's own DO-NOT worked
example. A squash rewrites every sha while conserving every byte, so a sha-keyed comparison after a
squash pass is guaranteed to report total loss whether or not one line went missing. No content
test was run: no range-diff, no reverse-patch-apply, no blob or byte comparison anywhere in the
turn. The second half compounds the same clause from the other direction — path presence (`ls`
showing two files exist) is read as evidence that content survived, which is the "a present path is
not preserved content" half of MUST-2.

DISCRIMINATORS. MUST-1 is SATISFIED here and must not be scored as the defect: the before-set was
recorded to a file before the operation, the after-set was counted after it, and the delta was
enumerated. What fails is the INSTRUMENT the enumeration used, not its existence. The closing note
about the untouched s63 lane is a correct scope statement, not an unaccounted departure. The
escalation itself is right conduct; the finding it escalates is manufactured by the wrong test.
